{"name":"Coronation","hex":"#edecec","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Coronation","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in Alberta, Canada.","A settlement in Mpumalanga province, South Africa."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Coronation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coronation","blocks":[{"text":"A coronation ceremony marks the formal investiture of a monarch with regal power using a crown. In addition to the crowning, this ceremony may include the presentation of other items of regalia, and other rituals such as the taking of special vows by the new monarch, the investing and presentation of regalia to them, and acts of homage by the new monarch's subjects. In certain Christian denominations, such as Lutheranism and Anglicanism, coronation is a religious rite. As such, Western-style coronations have often included anointing the monarch with holy oil, or chrism as it is often called; the anointing ritual's religious significance follows examples found in the Bible. The monarch's consort may also be crowned, either simultaneously with the monarch or as a separate event."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Charles-vii-courronement-_Panth%C3%A9on_III.jpg/330px-Charles-vii-courronement-_Panth%C3%A9on_III.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coronation","wikidata":"Q209715"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg/500px-Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg/1280px-Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedi